The second pass, on the file that exists. The full book was re-laid out under my first list (your 142 pages, then the release's 140), so its page numbers moved and I have rebuilt the list. This one is taken from the published PDF of the release made at 02:17 UTC on 4 November (140 pages), not from a build of my own: when I built the same inputs here I got 141 pages, one more than CI's 140.

How far my own build can be trusted: of the 13 tail and gap pages it flagged and the 13 the published file shows, 12 are the same page number; the only difference is at the very end of the book (chapter_end_spill on page 141 in mine, chapter_end_spill on page 137 in the published file). So up to about page 137 the two agree page for page. I will check the published file when there is one, and my own build when there is not; the chapter title is the safer way to find a page.

